# Copy to supabase/.env and fill in. Read by the Supabase CLI, not by Next.js —
# it resolves every env(...) reference in config.toml from here.
#
# The CLI looks for dotenv files in supabase/ first, then the project root, and the
# ambient shell environment beats both. supabase/.env is already gitignored by the
# root .gitignore's `.env*` rule.

# The Google OAuth client — the same one production uses. Google Cloud Console → APIs &
# Services → Credentials → your Web application client.
#
# That client also has to list http://127.0.0.1:54421/auth/v1/callback among its
# Authorized redirect URIs — docs/setup/local-development.md#one-time-setup says why
# adding it takes nothing away from production.
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET=
